# delphi-runtime test counts — EXACT values, checked by .githooks/pre-commit.
#
#     EXECUTED=<n>
#     SKIPPED=<n>
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS (2026-08-20). `f380085` deleted TWO tests —
# `the_tool_receives_its_approved_argv0` and
# `a_second_kept_fd_survives_a_second_exec_and_is_executable` — in a commit whose message
# describes only widening a THIRD test and renaming it. 135 lines left execute.rs and the
# removal was not mentioned anywhere. Nothing noticed: the pre-commit gate counts FAILURES,
# not tests; `.github/rust-test-count-baseline` is deliberately unrecorded (a workspace
# count cannot be produced off-CI), so the disappearance guard that exists for exactly this
# was inert. The consequence was measured five commits later — "the approved argv[0] never
# reaches the tool" survived the entire mutation audit, because its test was gone.
#
# EQUALITY, NOT A FLOOR — the reasoning in `.github/rust-test-count-baseline` applies here
# unchanged: a floor is satisfied forever by a test that starts SKIPPING, which is the
# disappearance the guard is for. Both numbers are recorded because EXECUTED alone is blind
# to a compensating pair (one test deleted while another stops skipping).
#
# PROTOCOL. Any change to either number — up OR down — updates this file IN THE SAME COMMIT,
# with the reason in the message. The hook prints the measured pair when it refuses, so the
# update is a paste, not an investigation. A DROP in EXECUTED needs the specific test named:
# removed on purpose, or started skipping? The second is a defect wearing the first's clothes.
#
# ENVIRONMENT-SPECIFIC, like its workspace sibling. Measured UNPRIVILEGED, where
# `an_approved_action_runs_with_the_tool_account_credentials` skips. On a root lane it
# EXECUTES, so the pair there is EXECUTED=115 SKIPPED=0 — point the hook at another file via
# DELPHI_TEST_COUNT_BASELINE rather than editing these values for one run.
#
# THE EXPECTED FAILURES LIVE HERE TOO (D0A-R11-02), one `RED=` line each, because the hook
# must check WHICH tests fail and not merely how many. Counting two allowed a red/green
# identity swap: fix an R9-02 test, break a security test, total still two. Both are checked
# — the set must match exactly AND the total failure count must equal the number of RED
# lines, since a failures block and a result line can disagree.
#
# NO `RED=` LINES MEANS A FULLY GREEN SUITE IS REQUIRED. When D0A-R9-02 is fixed, delete
# them in that commit; the hook then refuses any failure at all.
#
# Scope: `-p delphi-runtime --lib --bins`, which is what the hook runs.
EXECUTED=114
SKIPPED=1
RED=execute::tests::nested_interpreter_substitution_executes_unapproved_content
RED=execute::tests::same_inode_overwrite_executes_unapproved_content
